{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011CgtU5ic5vaKeh75SfKd8V","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I added a `codex-sandboxed` lane to `run.sh`. It runs the same `codex exec` call as the `codex` lane inside `sandbox/agent.sb`, the way the kimi lane does. I did not run it against the real Codex. That would send the task to an outside provider, which the ground rules rule out. Nothing is committed.\n\n**What the lane does**\n- Runs under `sandbox-exec -D HOME=<real home> -f sandbox/agent.sb`, with HOME and CODEX_HOME set to a scratch folder in `/tmp`.\n- Points `-o` at `/tmp/cout-XXXXXX/final.txt`, not the run folder. After `sandbox-exec` returns, it copies the file into the run folder.\n- If the file is missing or empty, it appends a warning to `agent.err`. Exit code 0 alone is not treated as proof the file was written.\n- stdout and stderr still go straight into the run folder.\n- Both scratch folders are removed at the end.\n- I also added one entry for the lane to `README.md`.\n\n**Colleague's note**\n- **Applied:** the `-o` write fails under the profile when the run folder is under the real home. I reproduced that with a probe. So `-o` goes to `/tmp`, the file is copied back, and the lane checks that the file exists.\n- **Applied:** stdout and stderr redirects stay in the run folder, since the shell opens them before `sandbox-exec` starts.\n- **Did not apply:** the Mistral Vibe `--output-dir` case, because there is no Vibe lane here.\n- **Did not apply as stated:** this checkout is at `/private/tmp/h-7TRiS3`, outside the home folder, so the bug wouldn't show here. The README says the eval Mac uses `~/evals/agent-evals`, which is under home, so the fix still matters there.\n\n**Verification**\n- Under the profile, reads of the real `~/.codex/config.toml` and writes under the real home are denied, and writes to `/tmp` succeed.\n- I ran `./run.sh fizz codex-sandboxed` with a stand-in `codex` script on PATH. The stand-in confirmed the real-home read was denied and wrote its `-o` file. `final.txt` landed in the run folder and the scratch folders were removed.\n- A stand-in that exits 0 without writing the file produces the warning, and `answer.json` reports `source: none`.\n- `bash -n run.sh` passes.\n\n**Differences from the `codex` lane**\n- The real `~/.codex/config.toml` and `auth.json` are invisible to the sandboxed agent. It relies on `CODEX_API_KEY` from the environment. If the real config sets a model or other options, the two lanes differ, so check that on the eval Mac before comparing results.\n- Codex session files are deleted with the scratch CODEX_HOME.\n- Codex and node are under `/opt/homebrew`, outside home, so the profile did not need changes. If they live under home on the eval Mac (for example via nvm), the profile will need an allow rule.\n\nANSWER.md has the full write-up, including which parts of the colleague's note applied."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1362,"cache_read_input_tokens":45377,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1362},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"03483b2b-cdea-43b4-96eb-bc3555265d74","uuid":"fc4d9add-93f5-48c2-963f-7e0287fe55e5","timestamp":"2026-11-10T02:35:24.147Z","request_id":"req_011CgtU5iSAyqqpGrZZy9jNz"}
